{"subjectId":"dsa-advanced","id":"recursion","title":"Recursion","group":"","order":3,"html":"<section class=\"block\"><h3>Rope Cutting Problem</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> n = 5, a = 2, b = 5, c = 1<br><strong>Output:</strong> 5<br><strong>Input:</strong> n = 23, a = 12, b = 9, c = 11<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef maxPieces(n, a, b, c):\n  if n == 0:\n    return 0\n\n  if n &lt;= -1:\n    return -1\n\n  res = max(maxPieces(n-a, a, b, c), maxPieces(n-b, a, b, c), maxPieces(n-c, a, b, c))\n\n  if res == -1:\n    return -1\n\n  return res + 1\n\nmaxPieces(n = 5, a = 2, b = 5, c = 1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Subset of a Given String</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> \"AB\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> \" \", \"A\", \"B\", \"AB\"<br><strong>Input:</strong> \"ABC\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> \" \", \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"AB\", \"BC\", \"AC\", \"ABC\"</p>\n</div>\n<p>Formula to Calculate : 2^n</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def sub(str1, curr, ind):\n  if ind == len(str1):\n    print(curr, end = \"\")\n    return\n\n  sub(str1, curr, ind + 1)\n  sub(str1, curr + str1[ind], ind + 1)\n\nsub(\"ABC\", \" \", 0)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Tower of Hanoi</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> n = 1<br><strong>Output:</strong> Move Disc 1 from A to C<br><strong>Input:</strong> n = 2<br><strong>Output:</strong></p>\n</div>\n<p>1. Move Disc 1 from A to B</p>\n<p>2. Move Disc 2 from A to C</p>\n<p>3. Move Disc 1 from B to C</p>\n<p>Rules :</p>\n<p>1. Only one Disc moves at a time</p>\n<p>2. No larger Disc above smaller</p>\n<p>3. Only the top Disc of a tower can be moved</p>\n<p>Pseudo Code:</p>\n<p>TOH(n-1, A, B, C)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>TOH(n-1, A, C, B)</li>\n<li>Move Disc n from A to C</li>\n<li>TOH(n-1, B, A, C)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>--&gt; TOH(n, Source, Auxiliary, Destination)</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def TOH(n, A, B, C):\n  if n == 1:\n    print(\"Move 1 from\", A, \"to\", C)\n\n  else:\n    TOH(n-1, A, C, B)\n    print(\"Move\", n, \"from\", A, \"to\", C)\n    TOH(n-1, B, A, C)\n\nTOH(2, 'A', 'B', 'C')</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Josephus Problems (Elimination Game)</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> n = 7, k = 3<br><strong>Output:</strong> 3<br><strong>Input:</strong> n = 8, k = 2<br><strong>Output:</strong> 0</p>\n</div>\n<p>-----------</p>\n<p>People: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]; k = 3</p>\n<p>Remove 3 → People: [0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6]</p>\n<p>Remove 6 → People: [0, 1, 3, 4, 6]</p>\n<p>Remove 2 → People: [0, 3, 4, 6]</p>\n<p>Remove 7 → People: [0, 3, 4]</p>\n<p>Remove 5 → People: [0, 3]</p>\n<p>Remove 1 → People: [0]</p>\n<p>-----------</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def jos(n, k):\n  if n == 1:\n    return 0\n  else:\n    return (jos(n-1, k) + k) % n\n\nprint(jos(7, 3))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Ierative Explanation\n\ndef josephus(n, k):\n    # Initialize people in the circle\n    people = list(range(0, n))  # 1-based indexing\n\n    # print(people)\n\n    index = 0  # Starting index\n\n    while len(people) &gt; 1:\n        # Calculate the index of the person to be removed\n        index = (index - 1 + k) % len(people)\n\n        # Print the current state of the circle and the removal\n        print(f\"Remove {people[index]} → People: {people}\")\n\n        # Remove the person\n        people.pop(index)\n\n    # Print the last remaining person\n    print(f\"Last remaining person: {people[0]}\")\n\n# Test case\njosephus(7, 3)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Subset Sum Problem</h3>\n<p>subset of {1, 2, 3} are {}, {1}, {2}, {3}, {1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> {10, 5, 2, 3, 6} ; Sum = 8<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2<br><strong>Input:</strong> {10, 20, 15} ; Sum = 0<br><strong>Output:</strong> 1</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def subset(arr, n, sum):\n  if n == 0:\n    if sum == 0:\n      return 1\n    else:\n      return 0\n\n  return subset(arr, n-1, sum) + subset(arr, n-1, sum - arr[n-1])\n\narr = [10, 5, 2, 3, 6, 8]\nsum = 8\nsubset(arr, len(arr), sum)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Print all Permutations of a String</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"ABC\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> ABC ACB BAC BCA CAB CBA<br><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"AB\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> AB BA</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef permute(s, i):\n  n = len(s)\n\n  if (i == n-1):\n    print(\"\".join(s))\n    return\n\n  for j in range(i, n):\n    s[i], s[j] = s[j], s[i]\n    permute(s, i+1)\n    s[i], s[j] = s[j], s[i]\n\ns = \"AB\"\npermute(list(s), 0)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure></section>"}